<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Zhangzong of Jin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1168–1208</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Wanyan Jing</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Zhangzong of Jin, Wanyan Jing, ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchen-jin-dynasty">Jurchen Jin dynasty</a> from 1189 to 1208. A grandson of Shizong, he was a calligrapher and patron of Chinese learning, and his reign marked the height of Confucian government, with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taihe-code">Taihe Code</a> of 1201. Floods and the shift of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a>'s course in 1194, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inflation">inflation</a> and costly wars on the steppe and against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a>'s 1206 offensive weakened the state.</p></div>
